    def WatchContracts(self, request, context):
        """── Live push streams (no REST equivalent) ────────────────────────────
        Authenticated; permission requirements match the corresponding read
        RPCs (none for WatchContracts, the same as the WS `contracts` stream;
        none for WatchOrder / WatchOrders, same as REST GET /order and GET
        /orders).

        Protocol invariants:
        1. The first message after subscribe is always SNAPSHOT (for
        WatchOrder on a still-pending order, its body has
        state == PENDING and order_id == 0).
        2. If the server falls behind, a fresh SNAPSHOT is re-emitted
        before live events resume. WatchOrder re-reads its order instead:
        a live order is re-sent as SNAPSHOT, a still-pending one as the
        PENDING SNAPSHOT, and an order that finished meanwhile as its
        terminal event (FILLED for the full-execution record, CANCELLED
        for any other INACTIVE, REJECTED), which closes the stream. The
        same re-read follows the gateway refreshing its order store (a
        resubscription to the exchange's order feed, an unacknowledged
        order written off, a settled contract cleared). On a re-read, an
        order the gateway no longer holds, or that is no longer in the
        caller's member scope, closes the stream with no further event.
        3. WatchOrder closes cleanly after a terminal FILLED / CANCELLED /
        REJECTED event. A watch opened on an order that has already
        finished (REJECTED, or INACTIVE for any reason) sends its SNAPSHOT
        and then closes.
        4. WatchContracts sends latest state, coalesced per contract on a
        100 ms tick: each UPSERT carries one contract as it stands, at a
        newer internal version than the last one sent for it, and a write
        that changes nothing sends nothing. A client that falls behind
        receives one fresh SNAPSHOT, never an older book.
        5. WatchContracts sends DELETE only for a contract it sent before, and
        stays open after it; it closes on server shutdown and on caller
        cancel.
        """
        context.set_code(grpc.StatusCode.UNIMPLEMENTED)
        context.set_details('Method not implemented!')
        raise NotImplementedError('Method not implemented!')

